Sometime toward the end of this week we will post Patch 6 on
comp.sources.games.

If everything goes as planned, Patch 6 will contain an overlay
scheme (under MS-DOS), enhancements to the Mac port, and the long
awaited doors display code which shows doorways, closed doors and
open doors differently.  It will also contain numerous bug fixes.
In addition, Patch 6 will contain some changes aimed at improving
slightly the survival chances of a starting character in the first 
few dungeon levels.

There is another bit of information.  As things now stand,
we intend Patch 7 (which will come out a month or so after Patch 6)
to be the last official patch of 3.0.  After Patch 7, we intend to
start working on version 3.1 which will contain some radical changes
as compared with 3.0.  

There are a few related bits of information:

There was a desire expressed on the net that 3.0 be re-posted whole.
Regretfully, we cannot satisfy this request -- it's too cosly.  Instead,
we accepted an offer by Bill Randle (moderator, comp.souces.games) to
place a set of NetHack 3.0 files with all patches applied in the archives
of uunet and saab.  It is a generous offer, and we are pleased to accept
it.  Once Patch 7 is out, we hope that other archives will do the same.

While there will not be another official patch to 3.0 after Patch 7, we
will remain as eager as ever to receive comments and bug reports, except
that these will lead to improvements in 3.1, not in 3.0.  Until then,
please make extra effort between now and Patch 7 to uncover defects in the
game.  We would like to leave behind for the public as stable and playable
a 3.0 as possible.

There will be a particular effort requested of you to help stabilize the
overlay scheme.  There is a continual problem for those who work on it with
the mutating of the code as they go.  It's a constant catch-up problem,
and there will be a gap in it in the overlay scheme included in Patch 6.
We will make sure that the overlay team will be the last to work on the
Patch 7 code before it is distributed so that a stable overlay scheme
survives with 3.0.

Your comments and suggestions will be appreciated.

For the development team,

-Izchak


